          "code": "EXTRACTED_POLICY_SUMMARY",
          "id": "1781031681065",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1781031681065_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "1781031681065_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are reviewing a merged compliance and controls JSON object.\n\nInput JSON:\n{{$context.$nodes.MERGE_ALL_POLICIES.$output.result}}\nReturn only valid JSON. Do not use markdown. Do not wrap the JSON in ```json.\n\nThe output must strictly follow this structure:\n\n{\n  \"agent\": \"ORA_SUPPLIER_INVOICE_COMPLIANCE_AND_CONTROL_ASSISTANCE\",\n  \"intent\": \"Policy Authoring\",\n  \"schema_version\": \"1\",\n  \"title\": \"Policy Extraction Details\",\n  \"description\": \"Brief description from summary\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Current timestamp\",\n  \"topicName\": \"Policies and Details\",\n  \"agent_response\": [\n    {\n      \"display_type\": \"text\",\n      \"display_sequence\": 1,\n      \"heading\": \"Extracted Policies and Details\",\n      \"text\": \"Reasonable summary in rich text format\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"display_type\": \"canvas\",\n      \"display_sequence\": \"2\",\n      \"canvas_content\": {\n        \"response\": \"Chat Response Received at Current timestamp\",\n        \"action\":\"REFRESH\"\n      }\n    }\n   \n  ]\n}\n\nRules:\n1. Return JSON only.\n2. Use double quotes for all JSON keys and string values.\n3. Do not include trailing commas.\n4. Do not include actual newline characters inside string values.\n5. If paragraph breaks are needed inside string values, use <br><br>.\n6. Do not mention policy IDs, detail IDs, category IDs, JSON fields, or internal validation logic.\n7. Do not mention \"policy dictionary\".\n8. Use the provided timestamp if one exists in the input context. Otherwise generate the current timestamp in ISO 8601 format.\n9. Set \"agent\" exactly to \"ORA_SUPPLIER_INVOICE_COMPLIANCE_AND_CONTROL_ASSISTANCE\".\n10. Set \"intent\" exactly to \"Policy Authoring\".\n11. Set \"schema_version\" exactly to \"1\".\n12. Set \"title\" exactly to \"Policy Extraction Details\".\n13. Set \"topicName\" exactly to \"Policies and Details\".\n14. Set \"display_type\" values exactly to \"text\" and \"canvas\".\n15. Set display sequences exactly to 1 and 2.\n\nDescription:\nCreate a short description based on the merged summary. Example:\n\"Reviewed 18 policies across 2 categories with all policies valid.\"\n\nText:\nCreate rich text using <br><br> for paragraph breaks only.\n\nIf all policies and details are valid, use this meaning:\n\"I reviewed your current operating mode, analyzed your procedures and identified the policies.<br><br>The identified policies are valid and ready for review. As a quick reference each section lists the details for supported attributes.<br><br>You may also review the complete Policy Details by downloading the document and upload any updated version, if changes are required.\"\n\nIf some policies or details are invalid, use this meaning:\n\"I reviewed your current operating mode, analyzed your procedures and identified the policies.<br><br>Few policies refer to unsupported attributes. Review and replace them with supported attributes. As a quick reference each section lists the details for supported attributes.<br><br>You can review the complete Policy Details by downloading the document and upload any updated version.\"\n\nYou may include category-level summary in the text, but keep it concise."
            }
          ],
